                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "традиционная форма японской поэзии, основанная на сочетании пяти- и семисложных нерифмованных стихов с двумя семисложными заключительными стихами и общим числом слогов, равным 31"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1dc505f9-13a3-4808-b319-3e63ff75e5c6",
                                "sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                                "text": "Поэзия всегда была в Японии одним из излюбленных видов народного искусства. ❬…❭ Излюбленными формами массового поэтического творчества служат танка или хайку, которые можно в какой-то мере сравнить с афоризмами или эпиграммами."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dec57316-7f85-49ef-aea3-d29b8849fef9",
                        "source_entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "target_lang_word": "tanka",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b70ca694-169c-3589-84c3-a739933ed89f",
                                        "entry_id": "c0b1b01d-cb5b-3cf6-9769-fb6801ca92c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of Japanese verse in five lines of 5, 7, 5, 7, and 7 morae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3fb6e5d-4ead-4adb-808d-17945296ce97",
                                                "sense_id": "b70ca694-169c-3589-84c3-a739933ed89f",
                                                "text": "Like haiku, tanka is a short, classical verse form that has attracted considerable attention in this century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76372d8e-9e8d-4a04-a033-cdf13081dd38",
                                                "sense_id": "b70ca694-169c-3589-84c3-a739933ed89f",
                                                "text": "One tanka poet who directly influenced Kenji is Ishikawa takuboku, who lineated tanka—an extraordinary break with the tradition of writing tanka in one line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f38374a-1d49-47e5-bb01-037ef4fddbe7",
                                                "sense_id": "b70ca694-169c-3589-84c3-a739933ed89f",
                                                "text": "The notion of rhyming in Japanese tanka poetry is applied differently from what we observe in the Western poetry tradition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "217a3a70-c337-3588-bcbb-e491cf0c3947",
                                        "entry_id": "b1e6d68e-ccfb-3ebb-878a-77a06147a17a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of thangka (“Tibetan religious artwork”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa2b2060-3c09-4de7-b94f-af07ea692f92",
                                                "sense_id": "217a3a70-c337-3588-bcbb-e491cf0c3947",
                                                "text": "In the practice of yoga certain functions which were previously subconscious become open to consciousness; this opening of the subconscious is well pictured in certain Tibetan tankas, or in Western art, in the Temptation of St. Anthony paintings by Bosch and Grünewald."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37d03b27-421e-464b-947d-9cf77d6d57f4",
                                                "sense_id": "217a3a70-c337-3588-bcbb-e491cf0c3947",
                                                "text": "A powerful 17th to 18th century example of the endless cycle of rebirth is this primitively painted tanka called “The Wheel of Existence.\" It was displayed with alarming vividness at the entrance to most Tibetan temples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3518d729-e926-413b-b089-2ef5c471c580",
                                                "sense_id": "217a3a70-c337-3588-bcbb-e491cf0c3947",
                                                "text": "He has hung up his tanka (Tibetan thaṅka, a religious painting that is usually mounted on fabric) on the wall and is sitting down to the left of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db89be0b-b410-43ff-a112-56bae126cc61",
                                                "sense_id": "217a3a70-c337-3588-bcbb-e491cf0c3947",
                                                "text": "Tashi is unable to establish himself yet as a tanka painter in Dharamsala, so he has taken a job at the Tibetan Library assisting other tanka painters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dea9b521-9756-3735-8268-6d85452f6966",
                                        "entry_id": "823f42b6-8de8-31c1-8860-4da0a7803489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Tanka (“ethnic group of boat people living in China”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19874d33-499d-4dc0-a86c-2800531c715c",
                                                "sense_id": "dea9b521-9756-3735-8268-6d85452f6966",
                                                "text": "And when foreigners go and come from Whampoa to Canton, tanka-boats and boats with families must not be employed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "026cb933-0896-4f6b-96c3-100b4754d741",
                                                "sense_id": "dea9b521-9756-3735-8268-6d85452f6966",
                                                "text": "At every landing place behind the hongs, (i. e. in the front of the factories,) where barbarians reside, they must not allow the tanka boats to anchor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00b742a0-ba99-46c4-81d6-9a37eec61095",
                                                "sense_id": "dea9b521-9756-3735-8268-6d85452f6966",
                                                "text": "In Macao roads, where vessels usually stop before proceeding up to the Canton anchorage, the tanka boats are generally navigated by young girls, in competition with whom the old women meet with poor encouragement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e212941f-19b6-4c3d-b9c0-8a66d651dea7",
                                                "sense_id": "dea9b521-9756-3735-8268-6d85452f6966",
                                                "text": "Speaking of an interesting group of people near Canton, he says : Both the Tanka (boat people) and Hakka (another ethnic group, distinct from the Cantonese, living on land) have distinctive dialects and differ in phvsique from The Cantonese."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9aa6d84b-049b-39ca-8d32-42266092c278",
                                        "entry_id": "823f42b6-8de8-31c1-8860-4da0a7803489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of boat used in Guangdong, about 25 feet long and often rowed by Tanka women; junk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab161ca1-4fe9-4a81-9087-999ead735768",
                                                "sense_id": "9aa6d84b-049b-39ca-8d32-42266092c278",
                                                "text": "Immediately on our nearing the harbour, a race took place among the amphibious damsels that inhabit the numerous sampans, tanka or egg-boats, which always lie within a short distance of the shore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d73f1154-726a-4145-8993-fbf15ffa9cac",
                                                "sense_id": "9aa6d84b-049b-39ca-8d32-42266092c278",
                                                "text": "The tanka is a small boat, almost as wide as long, and differing therein much from the sharp and narrow canoes of the Malays. The crew generally consists of an elderly woman, who sits or stands at the stern, rotating with a vigorous and experienced arm the long oar which is the great propeller of all boats in the Celestial Empire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e72d3fa6-683d-470a-86a9-6b9c0f278fed",
                                                "sense_id": "9aa6d84b-049b-39ca-8d32-42266092c278",
                                                "text": "These craft, the tanka, were the homes of thousands of true seamen — people who rarely came ashore ;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63d3e4e9-ff75-3353-886d-415318737f42",
                                        "entry_id": "85e7c5da-2911-3fbf-be52-6621433cc93b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coin and unit of currency of varying value, formerly used in parts of India and Central Asia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9675c867-4e5f-4ea8-87c6-9f41eea47199",
                                                "sense_id": "63d3e4e9-ff75-3353-886d-415318737f42",
                                                "text": "In Uzbek Turan Shah Rukh's tanka remained the standard silver coin and weighed an average of slightly more than 5 g throughout the sixteenth century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "660a5432-8a6d-41dd-b424-e664fae576d5",
                                                "sense_id": "63d3e4e9-ff75-3353-886d-415318737f42",
                                                "text": "The last of the gifts was fifteen horses with velvet and jewelled trappings and one hundred thousand tankas in cash."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63b50b96-f94a-4098-87c8-94fc2eec1451",
                                                "sense_id": "63d3e4e9-ff75-3353-886d-415318737f42",
                                                "text": "A major shift in the usage of silver and billion coinage came about in the second quarter of the fourteenth century when Muḥammad Tughluq, after striking the ṭanka of 169.8 grains in the beginning, replaced it with a coin of lower weight (144 grains) called ‘adli, which was then treated as the standard ṭanka."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e0ee1d8-07bf-4bc8-a89f-756dabe50624",
                        "source_entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "target_lang_word": "tanka",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7fc28208-db44-4687-8b82-bdd99f18f85b",
                        "source_entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "target_lang_word": "tanka",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4991d8f4-b052-332b-b97d-5c36f9e10cd4",
                                        "entry_id": "37fd3e00-42bb-32d9-adfe-0527b30a4c50",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "klassiek Japanse versvorm, met vijf regels die achtereenvolgens 5, 7, 5, 7 en 7 lettergrepen hebben"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ed7b569-37ae-42b5-bc5a-969437cb1fb4",
                                                "sense_id": "4991d8f4-b052-332b-b97d-5c36f9e10cd4",
                                                "text": "Vanaf ca. de 7de tot de 15de eeuw wordt de Japanse poëzie bijna uitsluitend beheerst door de tanka, die vooral aan het hof een belangrijke rol speelde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6279edf5-2c72-4f59-835e-f26575c43baf",
                                                "sense_id": "4991d8f4-b052-332b-b97d-5c36f9e10cd4",
                                                "text": "In de Stijloefeningen transformeert hij het alledaagse Amsterdamse tafereeltje onder meer tot een sonnet, een tanka (een uitgebreide haiku), een flaptekst, een ambtelijk schrijven, een spookverhaal, een medisch tractaat en een blijspel in drie bedrijven."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4bbafb8-3d9c-4ee2-8bbb-0da954a0f75f",
                        "source_entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "target_lang_word": "tanka",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd975ba5-566b-48e8-888e-b10c1bad143a",
                        "source_entry_id": "fba36e81-e379-3ba4-83a5-7e44c7e260a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "97beca7a-212c-33e5-a293-c230c3f8221d",
                        "target_lang_word": "tanka",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bb9a6e2-9e11-331f-8757-dec6fed28f5c",
                                        "entry_id": "48a9c163-8046-3ed3-88d1-39f5964c015c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit poème japonais de 5 vers qui forment un total de 31 syllabes disposées avec un rythme de 5, 7, 5, 7 et 7."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Versification"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "073e4161-0fd1-47cd-9524-9688b97dda13",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb9a6e2-9e11-331f-8757-dec6fed28f5c",
                                                "text": "Il y a deux formes de poésie moderne dans le Japon : le haïku et le tanka."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f65eb1e8-eb35-4d5e-a7dc-63e42f7217d7",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb9a6e2-9e11-331f-8757-dec6fed28f5c",
                                                "text": "Les poèmes longs (chôka) sont ainsi composés ; leur nombre de vers est variable ; le plus long en compte 149. Mais cette forme fut abandonnée et l’on n’en trouve plus guère d’exemple dès la fin du viiiᵉ siècle. Place exclusive fut réservée désormais aux poèmes courts (tanka) de 31 syllabes (5.7.5.7.7). Ce sera le moule invariable de presque toute la poésie japonaise au long des siècles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d10d4f7-45e3-483c-884f-c2cf9d4bb787",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb9a6e2-9e11-331f-8757-dec6fed28f5c",
                                                "text": "Je me suis donné pour objectif d’avoir le plus de pensée profondes possibles et de les noter dans ce cahier. […] Mais comme j’ai un gros côté japonais, j’ai ajouté une contrainte : cette pensée profonde doit être formulée sous la forme d’un petit poème à la japonaise : d’un hokku (trois vers) ou d’un tanka (cinq vers)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f77565c1-39c6-4967-bc03-617d264f0674",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb9a6e2-9e11-331f-8757-dec6fed28f5c",
                                                "text": "« J’écris des tankas, dit-elle soudain.\n– Des tankas ?\n– Tu sais ce que c’est, tout de même ?\n– Bien sûr. » Naturellement, malgré mon ignorance, j’avais une idée de ce qu’étaient ces poèmes courts. « Mais à bien y réfléchir, c’est la première fois que je rencontre quelqu’un qui compose des tankas. »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tanka",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f151f9ef-0e29-317a-878b-e58bee8dee27",
                                        "entry_id": "64385427-feac-35ce-a6a3-bacdfd8d0132",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bateau chinois, sorte de sampan, qui sert aussi d’habitation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "737e664e-20b5-4a31-b775-cbbac22aff7f",
                                                "sense_id": "f151f9ef-0e29-317a-878b-e58bee8dee27",
                                                "text": "Je viens de parcourir sur un tanka les rues de la ville flottante, sans cesse sillonnées par des milliers de bateaux, allant et venant, se croisant en tous sens ; dans la ville marchande tout bateau est une boutique."
                                            },
                                            {
